Proseware, Inc. adds the file .github/hooks/policy.json to Repo1. The script check-tool.sh inspects each tool call. When a call violates company policy, the call must be blocked without a prompt, both in Copilot CLI and in Copilot cloud agent sessions.

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "hooks": {
    "[[1]]": [
      { "type": "command", "bash": "./scripts/check-tool.sh", "timeoutSec": 30 }
    ]
  }
}
```

For a violation, check-tool.sh writes this output:

```json
{ "permissionDecision": "[[2]]", "permissionDecisionReason": "Blocked by policy" }
```

How should you complete the configuration? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.
